      "text": "I wrote the answer to `answer.txt`. I worked it out by hand from the spec and did not run the program.\n\nThe main thing to note is that `fn` values do not capture their surroundings. Inside a call, a name reads the call's own locals first and the globals otherwise. So a function returned from another function sees globals such as `n`, `k`, `c`, `f`, `g`, `op` and `a` as they are at call time. The parameters of the function that created it are not visible to it.\n\nThe line reads: `6 7 12 16 7 101 200 1001 35 7 1 42 42 43 70 20 5 0 0 30 2001 1001`",
